    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326-a2">

                <pb facs="0371" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg337"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 148.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pringle to Mr.
                            Munoz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States, Guatemala and Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1897-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                                1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note dated yesterday, the 29th.</p>
                <p>I am obliged to confess that it has caused me some surprise, as I am unaware of
                    any cause for the withdrawal of the exequatur of Mr. Florentin Souza, United
                    States consular agent at Champerico.</p>
                <p>Will your excellency kindly furnish me with the reason for this action on the
                    part of His Excellency the President?</p>
                <p>May I request you to furnish me with the information at your earliest
                    convenience. I will place Mr. Samuel F. Lord in charge of the United States
                    consular agency for the present.</p>
                <p>I embrace this opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. Lynch Pringle</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
